criteria:
Inclusion Criteria

* Male and female patients;
* Patients aged between 18 and 65 years at the time of surgery;
* Patients who underwent anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) reconstruction using the Over-The-Top (OTT) technique combined with posterolateral corner (PLC) reconstruction;
* Patients who underwent surgery between January 1, 2017, and December 31, 2025;
* Patients who underwent preoperative imaging examinations (MRI and, if applicable, X-rays) of the affected knee confirming the diagnosis of ACL and posterolateral corner injuries;
* Patients who underwent isolated ACL + PLC reconstruction or ACL + PLC reconstruction combined with additional procedures on the same knee (e.g., meniscal treatment or concomitant ligament injuries);
* Patients who provided written informed consent to participate in the study.

Exclusion Criteria

* History of fractures of the same limb requiring surgical treatment;
* History of posterolateral corner (PLC) injuries of the knee requiring surgical treatment;
* Patients younger than 18 years or older than 65 years at the time of surgery;
* Patients who did not provide informed consent;
* Patients who are no longer contactable.
